'''Lowkey''' (古我王, ''Ko-Gaō'') is a [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]]/[[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] variant of [[The Face]] that appears in [[Legend Stages]]. He was added in [[Version 7.3 Update|Version 7.3]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Lowkey
|image = E 423.png
|first appearance = '''UL''': [[Languid Lakeside|Sub-chapter 6 - Languid Lakeside]]
|latest appearance = '''ZL''': [[Proposal at Sea|Sub-chapter 16 - Proposal at Sea]]
|money drop = 3,000¢ - 11,850¢
}}

==Enemy==
Lowkey combines attributes of The Face, [[Shy Boy]] and [[Hannya]], with high health, rapid attacks, one knockback and long range, but extremely slow movement speed and low attack power. Like most other Relic enemies, he has a 100% chance of inflicting [[Curse|curse]], which combined with his range of 500 can be deadly under the right circumstances.

Similar to [[Othom]] and other long-ranged [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relics]], Lowkey's attack power is still relatively low; because of that and his sluggish movement speed, he will never be able to push far on his own.

==Strategy==
As with most Relic enemies, any short-ranged units that rely on [[:Category:Anti-Relic Cats|anti-Relic]]/[[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|Floating]] abilities should not be used due to the [[Curse]] effect, and those that should be used should either be [[Immune to Curse]], long-ranged units ([[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]], [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]], etc.), or tanky units with high DPS like [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island Cat]] and [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera]] [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cat]] [[Li'l Titan Cat (Special Cat)|variants]] that can survive Lowkey's fast, long-ranged attacks. Later in the game, you can also try to rush him down by using [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Cat Mask Doron]], [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N2]], and [[Superfeline (Normal Cat)|True Superfeline]] should you have it. Keep in mind that Lowkey's range of 500 means few non-[[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] units will be able to outrange him, and for those that can may they still need a stepping stone to hit him with piercing range.

